# Mobile Conventions

## Stack
- Expo + Expo Router; screens in `app/`.
- HTTP uses axios + axios-auth-refresh; server clients in `src/api/create-server-client.ts`.
- Tokens persist in `expo-secure-store`.
- OAuth browser flow uses `expo-web-browser` and deep links via `expo-linking`.
- PKCE helpers use `expo-crypto`.

## Key Constraints
- OAuth login uses `WebBrowser.openAuthSessionAsync`; `app/auth/callback.tsx` is a redirect stub.
- App deep-link callback is `kotel://auth/callback` (scheme `kotel` in `app.json`).
- SecureStore keys are scoped per server URL (`accessToken:<serverUrl>`, `refreshToken:<serverUrl>`).
- API auth uses `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>` headers (no cookie-based auth on mobile).
- `toMobileNetworkUrl(serverUrl)` may downgrade `https://` to `http://` for IPv4 LAN/dev use; no downgrade for production hostnames.
- Expo E2E automation is out of scope; follow manual testing in `apps/mobile/README.md`.

